      "title": "Mature systems are defined by what they refuse to do",
      "caption": "Best line in a systems thread all week: most architecture diagrams show what software *can* do — mature systems are defined by what they *refuse* to. Scope is the real design. Anyone can add a feature; knowing what to permanently say no to is the senior skill.",
      "format": "quote",
      "bestPlatform": "mastodon",
      "triggers": [
        "identity",
        "social-currency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "quote": "",
      "povText": "",
