      "keep": true,
      "score": 7,
      "vibe": "contrarian",
      "topic": "ai",
      "title": "Architecture as a noun is why your system is fragile",
      "caption": "Take from a systems thread: we treat 'architecture' as a fixed blueprint, but in complex systems fixity IS fragility. The diagram that never changes is the one reality has already outgrown. Architecture is a process you keep doing, not an artifact you ship once.",
      "format": "minimal",
      "bestPlatform": "mastodon",
      "triggers": [
        "identity"
      ]
    },
    {
